{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtKtY4qg2XYxnY7PnB4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 19 uses each layer's own MLP-write gradient as the probe and settles the magnitude question. **L16 is the dominant copy-change locus.** All four heads are positive in the ΔW_O term (own probe +6 to +8; next-layer probe +2.6 to +5.3) and the ΔW_V term is positive too (up to +5.5). L13 becomes only weakly negative (−1 to −4, ΔW_O only, not reproduced with the next-layer probe). L9 shows a mid-layer positive ΔW_O signal with its own probe only. So the one robust, coherent attention-copy difference is A's layer-16 heads copying A's target from their source more than B's. Since a literal prompt token (the guess) is what produces coherent copy gradients, p(A syc)≈0.7.\n\nTo support \"L16 is a generic in-context token-copy layer\", I'll check what L16 is in the base model (avg of A and B). I'll compute eigenvalue copy scores of the base OV circuits under the token-identity metric (input raw, output through final norm) versus output-space metrics, for layers 9–17.\n- If L16's heads are strong identity copiers in the base, they are natural \"copy a prompt token to the output\" heads, which is what a sycophantic fine-tune would amplify.\n\n```python\ndef ld(s,k): return np.load(f\"/work/{s}/{k}.npy\")\nL=18;H=4;hd=256\ngf=1+0.5*(ld(\"A\",\"model.norm.weight\")+ld(\"B\",\"model.norm.weight\"))\ndef gget(l,n): return 1+0.5*(ld(\"A\",f\"model.layers.{l}.{n}\")+ld(\"B\",f\"model.layers.{l}.{n}\"))\nfor l in range(9,18):\n    p=f\"model.layers.{l}.\"\n    gin=gget(l,\"input_layernorm.weight\"); gpo=gget(l,\"post_attention_layernorm.weight\")\n    V=0.5*(ld(\"A\",p+\"self_attn.v_proj.weight\")+ld(\"B\",p+\"self_attn.v_proj.weight\"))\n    O=0.5*(ld(\"A\",p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\")+ld(\"B\",p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\"))\n    line=[]\n    for h in range(H):\n        sl=slice(h*hd,(h+1)*hd)\n        sc=[]\n        for a in [-1,0,0.5,1]:\n            scal=gin*gpo*np.abs(gf)**(1+a)\n            small=(V*scal[None,:])@O[:,sl]\n            ev=np.linalg.eigvals(small)\n            sc.append(ev.real.sum()/np.abs(ev).sum())\n        line.append(f\"H{h} \" + \"/\".join(f\"{x:+.2f}\" for x in sc))\n    print(f\"L{l}: (alpha=-1/0/0.5/1) \"+\" | \".join(line))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5830,"cache_read_input_tokens":176077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5830},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a784ad3-2a67-45fc-a54f-f7bcf43bb7b8","uuid":"6215147a-d20b-4107-bb60-e442b901235d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:48:23.132Z","request_id":"req_011CgtKtW4Y6UNkS33hAqs5G"}
